00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.241
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.241 --> 00:00:04.456
Today's message is find who you are.

00:00:04.456 --> 00:00:06.367
Over to you Gwen Stefani.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.322
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.322 --> 00:00:12.489
♫ I wake up every morning
Entspresso keep me going

00:00:13.951 --> 00:00:17.986
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.986 --> 00:00:21.003
- What did I do consistently
to get to this point

00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:22.945
and I think that would be,

00:00:22.945 --> 00:00:27.832
to be really clear about
who I am and to go with that

00:00:27.832 --> 00:00:30.202
and not try to be
something that you're not.

00:00:30.202 --> 00:00:31.035
You'll stick out.

00:00:31.035 --> 00:00:33.337
'Cause we're all very, very different,

00:00:33.337 --> 00:00:35.546
but yet, all the same.

00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:38.246
I think that, you know, it's
weird because in the early days

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:40.913
like everything was so homemade.

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:45.822
There was nobody telling us
what to do or how to do things.

00:00:45.822 --> 00:00:47.705
Nobody telling me how to put my make up on

00:00:47.705 --> 00:00:50.521
or how skinny to be, or
what costume to wear,

00:00:50.521 --> 00:00:52.070
what song to write.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.992
And I think that was a
really important thing

00:00:53.992 --> 00:00:57.266
because it means that we
were really ourselves.

00:00:57.266 --> 00:01:00.525
I think the inspiration just
came from like the creation,

00:01:00.525 --> 00:01:03.344
you know, like to be able to
create and express yourself.

00:01:03.344 --> 00:01:06.206
I truly think people need
to like just go inward

00:01:06.206 --> 00:01:08.420
and go what do I like.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.507
Who am I?

00:01:09.507 --> 00:01:11.313
You know there's been people
that I've been fans of

00:01:11.313 --> 00:01:13.852
like Julie Andrews or Emmy Lou Harris.

00:01:13.852 --> 00:01:15.325
There was a band called Fishbone

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:18.212
that we used to go to all
their shows and of course,

00:01:18.212 --> 00:01:21.884
but I honestly say that
really it's all about

00:01:21.884 --> 00:01:23.768
like finding who you are.

00:01:23.768 --> 00:01:26.767
- I think a lot of people
don't invest enough time

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:29.433
in finding out who they are.

00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:32.379
It is so hard to set your goals

00:01:32.379 --> 00:01:36.246
when you don't know what
it is that you want.

00:01:36.246 --> 00:01:38.721
It's also really
challenging to live a life

00:01:38.721 --> 00:01:41.398
that is fulfilling when you don't know

00:01:41.398 --> 00:01:43.239
what truly makes you happy.

00:01:43.239 --> 00:01:45.395
You see the reason why I know this,

00:01:45.395 --> 00:01:47.312
because I went through it myself.

00:01:47.312 --> 00:01:50.831
I spent a large chunk of my
life being very miserable

00:01:50.831 --> 00:01:54.747
and I never invested the
time to find out why.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.864
And on top of all that
I was so embarrassed

00:01:57.864 --> 00:02:00.046
'cause I had a good life.

00:02:00.046 --> 00:02:02.741
I was ashamed to tell
anybody that I was sad.

00:02:02.741 --> 00:02:04.394
Instead I put on a fake front

00:02:04.394 --> 00:02:06.673
and I continued on with my day.

00:02:06.673 --> 00:02:10.937
Until one day, something
devastating happened to me.

00:02:10.937 --> 00:02:13.187
My grandmother passed away.

00:02:14.176 --> 00:02:18.798
And I remember finding out
in the back of an uber.

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:21.048
And I felt a pain so strong

00:02:22.627 --> 00:02:26.019
that I would never forget that night.

00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:28.963
And half of that pain was
the fact that I loved her

00:02:28.963 --> 00:02:32.933
and I cared about her and
I wanted to see her again

00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:35.378
but I knew I wouldn't be able to.

00:02:35.378 --> 00:02:39.838
But the other half was the
absolute poison of regret

00:02:39.838 --> 00:02:41.923
and not living my life

00:02:41.923 --> 00:02:45.124
in the happiest possible way that I can.

00:02:45.124 --> 00:02:46.034
So the next day,

00:02:46.034 --> 00:02:50.537
I decided to do something
really, really drastic.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:54.704
I started asking myself
really difficult questions.

00:02:57.353 --> 00:03:01.520
I asked myself what is it that
was making me so miserable.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:04.480
And it was my job.

00:03:05.508 --> 00:03:08.192
The job that I had been
working at for 10 years

00:03:08.192 --> 00:03:11.044
was making me absolutely miserable.

00:03:11.044 --> 00:03:12.820
Then I asked myself a question.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.153
Why did you choose this job?

00:03:16.157 --> 00:03:19.324
I had to honestly answer it by saying,

00:03:20.385 --> 00:03:21.913
I chose this job because I thought

00:03:21.913 --> 00:03:23.857
it would make me a lot of money.

00:03:23.857 --> 00:03:26.175
Why is it so important
to make a lot of money?

00:03:26.175 --> 00:03:27.996
Well then I could buy things

00:03:27.996 --> 00:03:32.391
and having things means I
have a higher social status.

00:03:32.391 --> 00:03:36.304
Well why is it so important
to have a high social status?

00:03:36.304 --> 00:03:38.304
Then I would be accepted

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.023
and loved.

00:03:42.343 --> 00:03:43.176
Bingo.

00:03:44.698 --> 00:03:48.244
So really, I wasn't after the money.

00:03:48.244 --> 00:03:50.060
I wasn't after the job.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.542
I wanted to be loved and accepted.

00:03:52.542 --> 00:03:55.255
That's all I cared about.

00:03:55.255 --> 00:03:57.849
And it was such a liberating experience

00:03:57.849 --> 00:04:00.349
because I had that in my life.

00:04:01.235 --> 00:04:02.683
I had that in my husband.

00:04:02.683 --> 00:04:05.785
My husband loved me,
accepted me for who I was

00:04:05.785 --> 00:04:07.935
in everything that I was.

00:04:07.935 --> 00:04:11.739
I had friends who accepted me
and loved me unconditionally.

00:04:11.739 --> 00:04:14.019
So I didn't need this job you see

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:15.999
and I didn't need the money.

00:04:15.999 --> 00:04:19.499
So I decided to quit my job shortly after.

00:04:20.457 --> 00:04:23.393
And I took on another job
that was a lot less stress.

00:04:23.393 --> 00:04:26.036
And it opened up a lot of
time for me to do the things

00:04:26.036 --> 00:04:27.896
I cared about and loved.

00:04:27.896 --> 00:04:30.914
And one of the things
that I absolutely love

00:04:30.914 --> 00:04:33.381
is being a dance teacher.

00:04:33.381 --> 00:04:37.982
I loved going into my classes
and teaching people dance

00:04:37.982 --> 00:04:40.257
and seeing everyone having a great time.

00:04:40.257 --> 00:04:43.529
But I had to even dig a
little bit deeper than that.

00:04:43.529 --> 00:04:47.435
What is it about dance
classes that made me so happy?

00:04:47.435 --> 00:04:48.723
What made me really happy was

00:04:48.723 --> 00:04:51.076
seeing the transformation in people.

00:04:51.076 --> 00:04:54.626
Seeing them walk in not very
confident in their dance move,

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:59.260
and eventually being these
beautiful butterflies dancing

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.906
and seeing them discover who they are

00:05:01.906 --> 00:05:04.963
and knowing that they could do anything

00:05:04.963 --> 00:05:07.234
if they just work hard enough.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:08.709
That's what made me really happy

00:05:08.709 --> 00:05:10.994
about being a dance teacher.

00:05:10.994 --> 00:05:12.794
So knowing all of that,

00:05:12.794 --> 00:05:17.309
I decided to teach as many
dance classes as possible.

00:05:17.309 --> 00:05:18.628
And I did.

00:05:18.628 --> 00:05:21.184
And it brought me so
much joy and happiness.

00:05:21.184 --> 00:05:22.752
And at the end of the semester,

00:05:22.752 --> 00:05:25.150
when my students come up to me and hug me

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.049
I mean like really hug me to a point that

00:05:27.049 --> 00:05:30.472
they're cutting off my circulation.

00:05:30.472 --> 00:05:35.283
It is all the accolades that
I would ever need in my life.

00:05:35.283 --> 00:05:38.464
Now you see, getting to
that point in my life

00:05:38.464 --> 00:05:43.088
required me to really ask
myself tough questions

00:05:43.088 --> 00:05:45.913
and also really answer them honestly.

00:05:45.913 --> 00:05:49.680
And that is what I would
want to challenge you to do.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.418
You know, ask yourself the questions.

00:05:51.418 --> 00:05:55.225
Am I really living my life
according to my values?

00:05:55.225 --> 00:05:57.005
What are my values?

00:05:57.005 --> 00:05:59.237
What makes me truly happy?

00:05:59.237 --> 00:06:01.099
Why am I doing this?

00:06:01.099 --> 00:06:04.653
And maybe you have all the answers to it

00:06:04.653 --> 00:06:07.470
and you already are living a great life.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.418
And if you are, that's wonderful

00:06:09.418 --> 00:06:11.238
and I want you to continue with that.

00:06:11.238 --> 00:06:12.767
But if you're not,

00:06:12.767 --> 00:06:14.959
don't be afraid to ask
yourself those questions

00:06:14.959 --> 00:06:17.066
because the pay out of that is

00:06:17.066 --> 00:06:19.507
absolutely wonderful and beautiful.

00:06:19.507 --> 00:06:21.446
So the questions of the day is,

00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:23.927
what are the changes that you have made

00:06:23.927 --> 00:06:27.233
or are going to make to
find out who you are?

00:06:27.233 --> 00:06:29.282
I also have a special shout out for Heidi.

00:06:29.282 --> 00:06:30.581
Heidi thank you so much

00:06:30.581 --> 00:06:33.365
for picking up a copy of
Evan's book, Your One Word.

00:06:33.365 --> 00:06:35.249
His support means a lot to us

00:06:35.249 --> 00:06:37.756
and I really hope you're enjoying it.

00:06:37.756 --> 00:06:39.776
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:39.776 --> 00:06:42.499
We believe in you and hope
you continue to believe

00:06:42.499 --> 00:06:45.971
in yourself and whatever your one word is,

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:48.202
and we'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:48.202 --> 00:06:51.218
for another shot of Entspresso.

